Tidy the module layout and draw the two diagrams

Housekeeping found one real dead import (units.js pulled projectsRoot and never
used it) and two pieces of duplication: the same best-effort JSON reader existed
in sync.js and sessions.js, so it moved to lib/json.js, and readSessionPage still
probed three request shapes although the contract was settled months of commits
ago — it now uses the address + closed throughSeq shape and returns records
instead of an attempt report.

docs/ gains two generated figures and their scripts: the two-machine component
map with a verification ledger, and the two decision flows (one sync tick, one
remote prompt). The Mermaid source lives in docs/architecture.md so the picture
is reviewable in a diff; the PNGs are rendered by docs/render-*.py because the
strings in them are facts that have to be re-derived when a port or a status
changes, not artwork. README's directory listing was also out of date: it had no
sessions.js, webdav.js, discovery.js, patch.js, atomic.js, client.js or tests.

No behaviour change beyond readSessionPage. Verified by node --check on every
module plus both test suites (30 + 12 cases); the diagrams were rendered and
read back. The running instance still executes the previous build string — the
profile reload watcher on this Windows install is dead until the app restarts.
